{"event_type":"review","id":"121c04d65b6730f216454da1510734661a470c1e8c6d1d51f9018e462875147f","occurred_at":"2026-11-22T11:54:25Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9dbef58a6d1682b25757b9f19d5b8ab5aa54e36788f30e085506956d72f503fe","sha256":"9dbef58a6d1682b25757b9f19d5b8ab5aa54e36788f30e085506956d72f503fe"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1ba53944d3ce64db73454b6947bfa63b293b69bdbcf6e801054d05777a66b7f8","sha256":"1ba53944d3ce64db73454b6947bfa63b293b69bdbcf6e801054d05777a66b7f8"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b952003f46321d879baa4836fae5e4b7a8729653c0bc94f5a4a32ba31987084e","sha256":"b952003f46321d879baa4836fae5e4b7a8729653c0bc94f5a4a32ba31987084e"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/83f40d0c4b6ba7d3b03671509e48d52f8c6124744ea0fc65880a368256d0e70e","sha256":"83f40d0c4b6ba7d3b03671509e48d52f8c6124744ea0fc65880a368256d0e70e"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/cbf8b6a035a523b6063504fa38b21ac1579c2d558c14c3c72c68fdc4d004b8d2","sha256":"cbf8b6a035a523b6063504fa38b21ac1579c2d558c14c3c72c68fdc4d004b8d2"}],"attempt_id":"e71c1d8868d5950d4a295ea833f2d106e7aa3f279c0ea9bbe88744b898de86f7:0:1","base":"9eebea8a942ff6a20b056504b570739f1948f620","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"e3ba46143ae5ae86990c4c13564bba86efb5fedb","body":"**Return JSON for argument errors.**\n\nAt apps/crq-python/tick_shadow_compare.py:214, omitting `--ts-plan` invokes argparse's default error handler. It prints usage to stderr and exits 2 without a JSON artifact on stdout. Python documents this default behavior. ([docs.python.org](https://docs.python.org/3.12/library/argparse.html?utm_source=openai))\n\nOverride the parser error path to emit the usage JSON object and preserve exit 2. Keep valid invocations unchanged.\n\nAs per coding guidelines, I1 requires: “Every operation invocation writes machine-readable JSON to stdout.”","id":"5c0f4d749385f7fa8de4b6230c98fe6ade4622546fc4e7b538d0c36c1602b3a1","intervals":[[214,214]],"path":"apps/crq-python/tick_shadow_compare.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Return JSON for argument errors."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"e3ba46143ae5ae86990c4c13564bba86efb5fedb","body":"**Map a missing frozen `config.json` to a `CompareError`.**\n\nWith a valid plan and no `config.json` under the runner root, `_oracle` raises `FileNotFoundError` at `shutil.copy2` (line 78). `main` catches only `CompareError`, so the exception escapes. The command prints no JSON error object and exits with status 1. The module docstring documents exit code 1 as \"differences found\" and exit code 2 as \"usage or input error\", so a caller can read a crash as a comparison result.\n\nConvert the read failure at this boundary:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    shutil.copy2(runner_root / \"config.json\", shim / \"config.json\")\n+    try:\n+        shutil.copy2(runner_root / \"config.json\", shim / \"config.json\")\n+    except OSError as exc:\n+        raise CompareError(f\"cannot read frozen config.json: {exc}\") from exc\n```\n\n</details>\n\nThe other filesystem reads in `_oracle`, such as the `python_root` copies, can raise the same exception. Handle them the same way. Keep unexpected programming errors outside this conversion.","id":"eba800af406e7323db2c0c862d295657ddf140222b2922b344f7b3b0aab62a8d","intervals":[[222,222]],"path":"apps/crq-python/tick_shadow_compare.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Map a missing frozen `config.json` to a `CompareError`."}],"head":"552eb5a30e24421f7f6455e460ca8594f10dfc9b","head_tree":"d16e28012af19cbe4667ce22a44fed8d3e652014","input_scope":[{"blob":"aa3db2fc941fc6bfd4ffc01c75b527d9423b71b3",